      "text": [
        " : سَأَلَ سَلَمَةُ بْنُ مُحْرِزٍ أَبَا عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ وَ أَنَا حَاضِرٌ فَقَالَ إِنِّي طُفْتُ بِالْبَيْتِ وَ بَيْنَ اَلصَّفَا وَ اَلْمَرْوَةِ ثُمَّ أَتَيْتُ مِنًى فَوَقَعْتُ عَلَى أَهْلِي وَ لَمْ أَطُفْ طَوَافَ اَلنِّسَاءِ فَقَالَ «بِئْسَ مَا صَنَعْتَ» فَجَهَّلَنِي فَقُلْتُ اُبْتُلِيتُ فَقَالَ «لاَ شَيْءَ عَلَيْكَ»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3130 - It is narrated from Mansur ibn Hazim, who said: Salamah ibn Muhraz asked Abu Abdullah (as) while I was present.\nHe said: \"I performed Tawaf around the Kaaba and between Safa and Marwah, then went to Mina and had relations with my wife without performing the Tawaf al-Nisa.\"\nAbu Abdullah (as) said: \"What a bad thing you have done,\" reproaching me.\nI said: \"I was put to trial.\"\nImam (as) replied: \"There is no penalty upon you.\""
        ]
      }
    },
